## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design an extensible runtime plugin system for distributed API clients, emphasizing idempotency and retry logic.

## Key Concepts

- **Strategy pattern**: Encapsulates retry algorithms in interchangeable objects
- **Runtime registry**: Enables registration and resolution of strategies by name without modifying core logic
- **Plugin-like extensibility**: Allows adding new strategies (ContentHash, TimeWindow, RandomizedDelay) at runtime
- **Idempotency semantics**: Ensures safe retry behavior for distributed systems

## Code Example

```typescript
interface IdempotencyStrategy {
  shouldRetry(request: Request, response: Response, attempt: number): boolean;
  backoff(attempt: number): number;
}

type StrategyFactory = () => IdempotencyStrategy;

class IdempotencyRegistry {
  private strategies = new Map<string, StrategyFactory>();
  private defaultStrategy: IdempotencyStrategy;

  register(name: string, factory: StrategyFactory): void {
    this.strategies.set(name, factory);
  }

  resolve(name?: string): IdempotencyStrategy {
    if (name && this.strategies.has(name)) {
      return this.strategies.get(name)!();
    }
    return this.defaultStrategy;
  }
}
```

